35,2,1,talk,George,,The other households blamed the constant asking. Our own checking felt like accusation. We must stop the favour cycle before it poisons us.,"{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Toshio,,"The diary shows Saturday usage is triple Tuesday’s. The mechanic confirms short runs damage the car. We need a rigid, simple schedule to stop the chaos.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Victoria,,"The mechanic’s warning confirms my fear. Short, cold runs are destroying the car. We need a protocol to prevent this daily wear.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Misaki,,"The fixed costs are 280,000 yen. Fuel usage is heavily skewed. We need a formula that accounts for both fixed and variable costs fairly.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Minato,,"I found the receipts. Two people bought most of the fuel, but the diary shows Saturdays are busier. I want to pay for what I actually use.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,George,,"@Toshio, a rigid schedule might just create new friction. The other households failed because of constant asking, not lack of rules.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Toshio,,"@George, rigidity prevents the asking. If the schedule is absolute, no one needs to negotiate. That removes the social debt entirely.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Victoria,,"@Toshio, a rigid schedule ignores the physical reality. If the car is already damaged by short runs, more driving just accelerates the failure.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Misaki,,"@Victoria, the car’s condition is separate from the money. I need to know if the 280,000 yen covers repairs, or if that’s a separate burden we’re ignoring.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Minato,,"@Misaki, I think the fuel receipts show who drives most. Maybe we should just pay based on that? It feels fairer than guessing.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,George,,"@Minato, paying by usage ignores the social cost. The other households failed because asking for favours felt like a burden, not just a transaction.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Toshio,,"@Minato, usage data is necessary, but it doesn’t solve the coordination overhead. I need to see how the administrative time correlates with the actual driving patterns.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Victoria,,"@Minato, usage data is cold. I need to know if the car is safe to drive before we calculate who pays for the privilege.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Misaki,,"@Minato, usage data is necessary, but it doesn’t solve the coordination overhead. I need to see how the administrative time correlates with the actual driving patterns.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Minato,,"@George, I hear you. But I just want the numbers to be true. If we know who drives, the paying feels less like a fight.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,George,,"@Minato, you are right. True numbers reduce suspicion. But we must also agree on a simple, low-friction way to request the car, so asking never feels like a burden.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Toshio,,"@George, I agree. A simple, fixed request method eliminates the negotiation. I will propose a strict, automated system to remove the human element entirely.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Victoria,,"@Toshio, automation won’t fix a car left with the fuel light on. I need a physical handover check, not just a digital log.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Misaki,,"@Victoria, I agree. We need a clear handover protocol. But let’s focus on the financial split first. How do we divide the 280,000 yen fixed costs fairly?","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Minato,,"@Misaki, I think we should split the fixed costs equally. The fuel part can follow the receipts. That feels simple and fair to me.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
